reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: How is the merge request contract enforced rather than merely instructed?

Records the decision that merge request bodies are judged by engsys vcs check-merge-request, called from a PreToolUse hook before gh pr create, instead of relying on a skill instruction.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; frontmatter including superseded-in-part-by: 0025 is unchanged, as are the PR #20/#21/#22 incident, the --body-file rule and the five rejected alternatives.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
Contract keys (section-heading-prefix, forbidden-body-contains, writing, excluded) and commands kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.
The limitation that writing style is not machine-judged is kept as stated.

